      "id": "yeats-collected-poems-s0190-p00407",
      "source_en": "Labour is blossoming or dancing where\nThe body is not bruised to pleasure soul,\nNor beauty born out of its own despair,\nNor blear-eyed wisdom out of midnight oil. 6o\n0 chestnut tree, great rooted blossomer,\nAre you the leaf, the blossom or the bole?\n 0 body swayed to music, 0 brightening glance,\nHow can we know the dancer from the dance?",
